From ac676cbc756c1117797aad7f65fa7b86f91256da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:34:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] wsi: read sw frames back through cached memory,
 invalidate first (PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED)

On kbase without the DRI3 dma-buf path PanVK is a sw WSI device, so
every X11 present (PanPlay's Wine/DXVK games) copies the frame on the
CPU: the GPU blits the swapchain image into a linear buffer, and
x11_present_to_x11_sw() memcpys that buffer into the MIT-SHM segment
(or hands it to PutImage).  wsi_select_host_memory_type() asks for
HOST_COHERENT|HOST_CACHED and, finding none on a GPU that is not IO
coherent, falls back to HOST_COHERENT alone.  On PanVK that is memory
type 1, the uncached (write-combined) kbase mapping, so the CPU reads
3.6 MB per frame at 1280x705 (10.4 MB at 2400x1080) with no line fills
and no prefetch, roughly 3.5 ms per present at ~1 GB/s.

Add wsi_device::sw_cached_noncoherent.  When set, buffers that only this
process reads back through wsi_image::cpu_map (no alloc_shm, so no
other process maps them) prefer HOST_COHERENT|HOST_CACHED as before,
then HOST_CACHED without COHERENT, then the old choice.  The image
records whether its cpu_map memory is coherent, and
wsi_image_invalidate_cpu_map() calls vkInvalidateMappedMemoryRanges
(new WSI_CB) over the whole range before each CPU read: in
x11_present_to_x11_sw() and in the Wayland SHM memcpy path, both after
the blit fence has signalled.  Memory that a foreign process reads
directly (alloc_shm / host-pointer import) keeps the coherent type.
The GPU side is unchanged: the blit's TRANSFER_WRITE -> HOST_READ
barrier already cleans the GPU L2 before the fence signals.

PanVK sets the flag in panvk_wsi_init() from PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED
(default 1), a bit of P-A's panvk_perf_knobs registry: resolved once
at the first vkCreateInstance with os_get_option() (so a debug.mesa.*
property works on Android) and named in the "114 behaviour restored
for:" log line when 0.  panvk_InvalidateMappedMemoryRanges() does the
kbase sync (userland DC CIVAC by default) and the closing barrier.  On an
IO-coherent system the cached coherent type exists and is still taken,
so nothing changes there.

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26 C2 (a), "X11 software present: CPU
read from write-combined memory and a blocking round trip per
present".  Knob: PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=0 restores the 114 behaviour (the
uncached coherent buffer, no invalidate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
